# Build outputs
# Root-anchored: rattler-build's path source copy honors .gitignore, and an
# unanchored build/ would drop the tracked thirdparty/libtiff/build/ directory.
# Build trees. `build/<name>` is the convention (okf/specs/build-tree-layout.md)
# and CMakePresets.json and scikit-build-core already follow it -- but nothing
# enforces it, so the ad-hoc names are ignored too. The root once carried eight
# trees at 1.7 GB, and `build_*` matched none of the rules that existed then:
# 480 MB of object files were offered as untracked files next to the sources.
/build/
build-*/
build_*/
cmake-build-*/
bld-dir/
dist/
dist
*.whl
wheelhouse/
wheelhouse_*/
build_log.txt
debug_*.py
doc/auto_examples
tmp/
.venv
.boost_env
playground
junk/
venv
# root-level build/install copy only — must not match nested package dirs
# such as ext/**/io/github/fluorescencetools/tttrlib/ or ext/python/tttrlib.*
/tttrlib
!bin/tttrlib

# Local planning and agent state
.omx/

# AI coding tools (assistant state, caches, local config)
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.codeium/
.continue/
.copilot*
.gemini*
.crush/
.windsurf/
.tabnine*
.idx/
.zed/

# Windows artifacts
nul

# CMake builds
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeScripts/
# Anchored: unanchored `Testing/` matches at any depth, and this filesystem is
# case-insensitive, so it silently swallowed okf/testing/ -- benchmarking.md
# and three test files were untrackable for as long as the rule has existed.
# CTest only writes this under a build directory, and those are ignored above.
/Testing/
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json
CTestTestfile.cmake
DartConfiguration.tcl
install_manifest.txt
_deps/

# Local ImageJ/Fiji plugin build & launch folder (native libs, ij.jar, jars)
imagej-test/

# Conda/rattler build output
conda-bld/
docsenv/

# act cache
.act-cache/

# Local tooling state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Documentation and tools
doc/_*
doc/xml
doc/_build/
doc/paper*
/doc/examples/
doc/sg_execution_times.rst

# IDE
.vscode
.vs
.idea/
.cache

# Python
__pycache__
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.benchmarks/
.ipynb_checkpoints
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Test data
tttr-data
test/tttr-data

# Scratch and temporary
leftovers/
temp/
optimization-docs/

# Test diagnostics (generated by test runs)
test/diagnostics/*.png

# prototype/ is for prototyping, not for the pictures a prototype prints.
# validate.py writes validation_visual.png next to itself and it was committed.
prototype/**/*.png

# Scratch scripts. Working *notes* do not belong here: findings go in okf/, and
# SIM_INTEGRATION_NOTES.md sat at the root ignored by this list for two months
# with three reproducible gotchas in it that nobody could see.
/scratch_bench_sim.py
# Scratch data written by examples/tests
examples/tttr/conv1.spc

# Benchmark suite: scripts + rendered plots are tracked; the local venvs, logs,
# and regenerable result data are excluded by benchmarks/.gitignore.
/benchmarks/.venvs/
/benchmarks/logs/
/benchmarks/results/

# ImageJ plugin: CMake-generated SWIG proxies and JNI natives are staged into the
# Maven source roots before `mvn package` (locally and in CI); never commit them.
ext/java/imagej/target/
ext/java/imagej/src/main/java/io/github/fluorescencetools/tttrlib/*.java
ext/java/imagej/src/main/resources/native/

# Java library module: CMake-generated SWIG proxies and JNI natives are staged
# into the Maven source roots before `mvn test`/`mvn package`; never commit them.
ext/java/pkg/target/
ext/java/pkg/src/main/java/io/github/fluorescencetools/tttrlib/*.java
ext/java/pkg/src/main/resources/native/

# JavaScript binding: npm's dependency tree, and the built addon plus the module
# libraries staged next to it. `npm install --prefix ext/js/pkg` fetches the
# Node-API headers; the .node is a build artefact of BUILD_JAVASCRIPT_INTERFACE.
node_modules/
ext/js/pkg/*.node
ext/js/pkg/*.dylib
ext/js/pkg/*.so
ext/js/pkg/*.so.*
ext/js/pkg/*.dll
ext/js/pkg/package-lock.json
# scripts/prebuild.mjs output (one directory per platform triple) and the
# directory scripts/pack.mjs assembles for publication. Both are release
# artefacts built by CI from source; nothing in them belongs in the repository.
ext/js/pkg/prebuilds/
npm-package/

# The naming repository, pulled at run time -- CI checks out
# Fluorescence-Tools/mmfdb here and points MMFDB_DIC_DIR at it, and a developer
# reproducing a run does the same. It is the vocabulary authority, never
# content of this repository: committing it is the one thing
# test_vocabulary_matches_mmfdb exists to prevent.
.mmfdb/

# The CLI and the examples write their output to the working directory, which
# for anyone running them from a checkout is this one. Root only: the real
# containers live under test/data and tttr-data, and none is tracked here.
/*.pto
/*.ptu
/*.png
/extracted_*/
build-r-*.log

.DS_Store
